+## Level transitions (Office | Level 0 borders)
+
+Red, 2026-10-21: **a Frame on every zone border, Renovation on about 3 in 10 crossings, the colour stays V5.** The map owns the rule and the collision; the visual kit (`FrontRoomsTransitionKit`, visual-owned) draws the pieces.
+
+- **Frame** (every Office | Level 0 edge, built by the kit; the Office, the newer fit-out, owns each piece): a portal on an open edge (0.12 × 0.20 pilasters, a header a bulkhead deep, a satin binder bar), a cased arch (the wall pieces beside it stop `BeadInset` short, render only), a double-acting pressed-steel sleeve and a 12 mm saddle at a door (D1.6's DA envelope, no stop), main's `DressWindow` frame at a window, end caps and corner guards, and a 0.10 rubber base on every Office wall face (outlets: `WallFace.baseTop` 0.10, so plates keep `BaseClear` above it). Where border open edges meet with no wall, a free post stands at the lattice point (0.20, or 0.24 in an arcade) **with a collider**: the only collision the kits add.
+- **Renovation:** `BorderRenovated(a, b)` is the one decision: an Office | Level 0 open, arch, door or window edge, neither cell excluded (`TransitionExcluded`: the start area, the exit area and the EXIT's 2-cell hold zone), drawn per crossing as `Unit(MapHash(seed, edge key, 977)) < renovationShare` (0.30). No revision, tier or build order, so both chunks, rebuilds and revisit shifts agree while the edge stays a crossing. The kit then strips, primes or paints the Level 0 drops within 2.25 m, cuts the carpet back to the slab and opens the ceiling (render only: the slabs keep their collision), and leaves an unfinished portal on a renovated open edge. Measured over 20 seeds × 81 chunks: 2.96 crossings and 0.92 renovated per chunk (31.2 %).
+- **Hooks** (`// TRANSITION` in `FrontRoomsMapWorld.cs`): `BuildInto` begins the chunk's kit, hands it each cell's slabs, each edge (with the opening as `BuildEdge` built it), each wall piece and each lattice point, and finishes it before the block renderers; a piece the kit renders keeps the map's own collision boxes, unchanged and in the same order. `transitions = false` builds exactly as before. Tools: `-transitionsOff` (with B0), `-transitionKitsOff`, `-transitionFrameOnly`, `-renoShare F`.
+- **Excluded** (`TransitionExcluded`, the kit's `excluded` view): the start area, the exit area X (so the EXIT door edge N | X) and every cell within 2 (Chebyshev) of the EXIT's N cell, where C23 mounts the LIT sign; the kit leaves them exactly as the map builds them (renovation never; frames only where the edge is a plain border). Add X1/X2 with the walkable stair and station rects (M4) once they exist. The kit reads edges through `EffectiveEdge`. Codex C3's post table takes over the posts (`PostAt`) when it lands.
